# Redoubt delete-on-quit-swipe.patch  (Android, LW-M7-45)
#
# Owner report 2026-10-06: "when swiping away the app, the delete all on close
# does not trigger. closing it with the close button, works". Owner decision
# 2026-10-06, verbatim: "lets build both as fallback".
#
# Upstream files touched
# -----------------------
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml          (one <service>)
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt
#       setupEarlyMain: DeleteOnQuitGuard.onColdStart() right before
#       restoreBrowserState()/restoreDownloads(); both wait for its gate.
#       setupPostMegazord: a ProcessLifecycleOwner ON_START observer.
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuDialogFragment.kt
#       the Quit callback also calls DeleteOnQuitGuard.onSessionEnding("quit").
# New files
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/lw/DeleteOnQuitGuard.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/lw/DeleteOnQuitGuardTest.kt
# Every hunk's context is identical in Firefox 157.0 and 158.0b3 (158 moved
# the Quit callback from onDeleteAndQuit to handleNavigationEvent, and added
# tabDataCoordinator.initialize() before restoreBrowserState; neither is in
# a context line). Fully qualified names are used instead of imports because
# the import blocks differ between the two.
#
# What upstream does
# -------------------
# "Delete browsing data on quit" (Settings) deletes the selected categories
# only from the menu's Quit item: DefaultDeleteBrowsingDataController
# .clearBrowsingDataOnQuit, then finishAndRemoveTask(). Swipe-away from
# recents, OOM kill, crash, force-stop and reboot skip it, and the next cold
# start restores the session (FenixApplication.restoreBrowserState) with the
# cookies, history and tabs the user asked to have deleted. Redoubt turns the
# feature on by default (privacy-defaults.patch: cookies + cache), so this hits
# every default install.
#
# What this patch does
# ---------------------
# (b) the guarantee. A marker file (noBackupFilesDir/redoubt_session_end,
#     written temp + fsync + rename) says how the session ended. It reads
#     "clean" only after Quit's deletion was confirmed by every store and by
#     Gecko; a cold start, a return to the foreground, and anything that kills
#     the process leave "running". On a cold start with the setting on and a
#     marker that is not "clean" (or absent), onColdStart:
#       1. writes "cleaning", attempt n, BEFORE deleting anything;
#       2. dispatches the Gecko deletions (StorageController clearData with the
#          upstream flags per category) synchronously from Application.onCreate,
#          i.e. before any activity or GeckoSession exists, so Gecko runs them
#          ahead of any page load, including one from a VIEW intent;
#       3. deletes the local stores on the IO dispatcher -- session file +
#          thumbnails (TABS), Places + recently closed tabs (HISTORY),
#          downloads DB (DOWNLOADS) -- while the main thread waits for them,
#          bounded (5 s). Only the wait is on the main thread: a step that
#          needs it cannot deadlock start-up (Fenix's PermissionStorage does:
#          it is backed by Gecko's site-permission storage, so it runs with the
#          Gecko deletions in step 2's async half; found on the device);
#       4. returns a gate that restoreBrowserState() and restoreDownloads()
#          join; it opens when Gecko and every store confirmed (bounded, 20 s),
#          and then the marker becomes "running".
#     A deletion that kills the process cannot loop: after 3 attempts that did
#     not finish, the start continues without deleting and logs an error; the
#     next unclean exit counts from 1 again. With the setting off nothing is
#     deleted, whatever the marker says. Private tabs are never persisted and
#     their Gecko data dies with the process; the selected categories are
#     cleared for normal and private browsing alike, as on Quit.
#
# (a) best effort. DeleteOnQuitTaskService, a started (not foreground) service
#     with stopWithTask="false" and no notification, is started at every
#     ProcessLifecycleOwner ON_START while the setting is on. When the task is
#     swiped away while it runs, onTaskRemoved starts the same deletion
#     without blocking (no ANR) and marks "clean" only if it finishes and the
#     app did not come back meanwhile. Android usually kills a background
#     process right after removing its task, and stops background services
#     about a minute after the app left the foreground, so (a) is measured,
#     never relied on; (b) covers everything (a) misses.
#
# Quit itself is unchanged; after upstream's deletion it also runs the guard's
# awaited deletion (idempotent) and only then writes "clean", because upstream
# does not wait for Gecko's clearData callbacks before finishAndRemoveTask().
#
# No network: every step is a local store or Gecko's StorageController.
# Log tag: RedoubtDeleteOnQuit (Logger info/warn/error reach logcat in
# release builds through FenixLogSink).
#
# Unit tests: DeleteOnQuitGuardTest (JVM, no Robolectric): marker atomicity and
# parsing, the cold-start decision table, ordering (attempt recorded before
# deletion; restore gated on the engine), bounded retries, timeouts, a local
# step that never returns (the main thread is released), the
# clean-quit / foreground race, setting off. The deletion itself is proven on
# a device: docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-45/.
#
