+// Redoubt LW-M7-45: "Delete browsing data on quit" also covers sessions that
+// did not end through the Quit menu item.
+//
+// Upstream deletes the selected categories only when the user picks Quit
+// (MenuDialogFragment -> DeleteBrowsingDataController.clearBrowsingDataOnQuit).
+// Swiping the app away from recents, an OOM kill, a crash, a force-stop or a
+// reboot skips the deletion, and the next start restores the tabs, cookies and
+// history the user asked to have deleted. Owner decision 2026-10-06: "lets
+// build both as fallback".
+//
+//   (b) the guarantee. A marker file records how the session ended: "clean"
+//       is written only after Quit's deletion has been confirmed; every other
+//       end leaves "running" (or "cleaning") behind. On a cold start with the
+//       setting on and a marker that is not "clean", FenixApplication runs the
+//       same deletion for the selected categories before the session store and
+//       the downloads list are restored: the engine deletions are dispatched
+//       to Gecko before any activity exists (so before any GeckoSession can
+//       load a page), the app-side stores (Places, session file, recently
+//       closed tabs, thumbnails, permissions DB, downloads DB) are deleted
+//       synchronously, and the restore waits for Gecko to confirm. A deletion
+//       that itself kills the process cannot loop: the attempt count is in the
+//       marker, written before the deletion starts, and after MAX_ATTEMPTS the
+//       start continues without deleting and logs an error.
+//
+//   (a) best effort. DeleteOnQuitTaskService (stopWithTask="false") is started
+//       while the app is in the foreground, so Android calls onTaskRemoved when
+//       the task is swiped away. That starts the same deletion without waiting
+//       for it; Android usually kills the process within milliseconds, so (a)
+//       may not finish -- (b) does not depend on it.
+//
+// Nothing here touches the network, and with the setting off nothing is
+// deleted. Log tag: RedoubtDeleteOnQuit.
